---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import LegalIdentity from '../../components/LegalIdentity.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, LAST_UPDATED, LEGAL, SITE_URL, CLARITY_ID, LANG_TAGS } from '../../data/site-config';
import { displayDate } from '../../lib/format';
import { route } from '../../i18n/routes';
const lang = 'en';
---
<PageLayout title="Privacy on US VIN Decoder: Your VIN Goes to NHTSA Only" description="Privacy policy of US VIN Decoder: no account, no cookie, no email asked. A VIN you type is sent by your browser to NHTSA and fueleconomy.gov only, never stored by us." lang={lang} noindex={true} breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Privacy' }]} showAuthor={false}>
  <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none prose-headings:font-serif">
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p>This policy covers {SITE_URL}. Many VIN check sites ask for an email or a card before showing a result, and use the VIN and the address to sell reports or pass leads to dealers. This site asks for neither. The publisher is established in France, so the EU General Data Protection Regulation governs everything the site does, for every visitor; residents of US states with a consumer privacy law keep at least the rights below.</p>
    <p>This site sets no cookie and stores nothing on your device.</p>
    <h2>1. Who is responsible</h2>
    <LegalIdentity lang={lang} />
    <h2>2. What happens to a VIN you type</h2>
    <p>The structure of the VIN (check digit, model year, maker code) is read in your browser, with no network request. When the 17 characters are complete, your browser sends the VIN directly to the National Highway Traffic Safety Administration (vpic.nhtsa.dot.gov and api.nhtsa.gov) and, with the make, model and year it returns, to the Department of Energy and EPA site fueleconomy.gov. These are US government services with their own privacy policies; they receive the request like any visit to their sites, including your IP address. The VIN never reaches us: the site is a set of static pages with no server code and no database. A VIN alone does not identify a person, but it can be linked to one through title records, so share links carefully.</p>
    <p>After you type, the address bar may show the VIN or the model you looked up, so that you can copy a link to the result. That link stays on your device unless you share it.</p>
    <h2>3. What else is processed</h2>
    <h3>Hosting logs</h3><p>GitHub, which hosts the pages, records the IP address, time, page and browser type of each request to keep the service secure. Legal basis: legitimate interest. Retention follows GitHub's policy.</p>
    {CLARITY_ID
      ? <><h3>Stability monitoring without cookies</h3><p>To find broken pages and scripts, the site loads Microsoft Clarity in its cookie-free mode: errors, loading times and clicks are measured per page view, without cookies and without linking visits; page content and everything you type, VINs included, are masked. Legal basis: legitimate interest in a working site (Article 6(1)(f) GDPR). You can object by blocking clarity.ms.</p></>
      : <><h3>No analytics today</h3><p>No audience measurement, advertising or social media tool is loaded. If a stability monitoring tool is added, this page will name it and say what it records before it is switched on.</p></>}
    <h3>E-mails</h3><p>If you write to us, we keep your address and message to answer, and delete them three years after the last exchange. You never need to send a VIN to report an error: the campaign number or the model is enough.</p>
    <h2>4. No sale, no leads</h2><p>We sell no data, share none with dealers, insurers or history report companies, and build no profiles.</p>
    <h2>5. Transfers</h2><p>The host and the government services queried by your browser are in the United States; hosting data may be processed there under the EU-US Data Privacy Framework.</p>
    <h2>6. Your rights</h2><p>Access, correction, deletion, restriction, portability and objection: write to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>, we answer within one month. You may also complain to the {LEGAL.supervisoryAuthority} (<a href={LEGAL.supervisoryAuthorityUrl} rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">{LEGAL.supervisoryAuthorityUrl}</a>).</p>
    <h2>7. Children</h2><p>The site is meant for adults buying, owning or servicing a vehicle and collects nothing from children.</p>
    <p>See also the <a href={route('cookies', lang)}>cookies page</a> and the <a href={route('terms', lang)}>terms of use</a>. Updated on <time datetime={LAST_UPDATED}>{displayDate(LAST_UPDATED, LANG_TAGS[lang])}</time>.</p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
